// HOLE 2 repro — pure stdlib, self-contained.
// A call in CONTINUATION position whose string arg contains `//` (a URL, a path,
// a comment marker as literal data) inside parentheses is mis-parsed: the
// invocation-argument paren-balancer treats `//` as a line-comment start even
// though it is inside a double-quoted string literal, swallows the closing `)`,
// and reports a false "unbalanced parentheses".
//
// EXPECTED: shape-checks (the string "(a//b)" is ordinary data).
// ACTUAL:   error[PARSE003]: unbalanced parentheses in invocation arguments
//
// Control (passes): replace `//` with `:` -> "(a:b)" shape-checks fine.
~import std/io
~import std/string
~std/string:from-page(text: "hi")
| ok s |> std/io:print.ln("(a//b)")
| err _ |> _
